You see a shaggy, scary beast with saber sharp teeth on the cover of the book. You skim through the pages. Aha, here is some information about it:
"...this beast, that travellers called a saber-toothed wolf - is one of the largest predators of Wild Island. It is primarily nocturnal animal. Tough fell and thick layer of subcutaneous fat serve as fine armour, capable to stop a rifle bullet. Intolerant to loud and shrill sounds. It is also unable to climb a tree that can save an unlucky wayfarer who came across this creature."
You close the book and shiver. It's better to steer clear of such a beast...